EXPERIMENT 22 – BOUNDARY VALUE ANALYSIS (MANUAL TESTING)
AIM
To create test cases for a student grade evaluation system using Boundary Value Analysis (BVA).

Boundary Value Analysis tests values at the edges of input ranges because defects occur more often at boundaries.
ALGORITHM
1. Study the grade rules: A (90–100), B (80–89), C (70–79), D (60–69), E (50–59), F (0–49).
2. Identify the lower and upper boundaries of every grade range.
3. Select values just below, on and just above each boundary.
4. Prepare test cases with marks, boundary tested and expected result.
5. Remove duplicate values and add invalid values -1 and 101.
6. Execute the test cases and compare actual and expected grades.
7. Record the test status.
INPUT – GRADE BOUNDARIES
Grade	Range	Min-1	Min	Min+1	Max-1	Max	Max+1
F	0–49	-1	0	1	48	49	50
E	50–59	49	50	51	58	59	60
D	60–69	59	60	61	68	69	70
C	70–79	69	70	71	78	79	80
B	80–89	79	80	81	88	89	90
A	90–100	89	90	91	99	100	101

TEST CASES
TC ID	Marks	Boundary Tested	Expected Result	Status
TC01	-1	Below minimum	Invalid marks message	Pass
TC02	0	Minimum	Grade F	Pass
TC03	49	Upper boundary of F	Grade F	Pass
TC04	50	Lower boundary of E	Grade E	Pass
TC05	59	Upper boundary of E	Grade E	Pass
TC06	60	Lower boundary of D	Grade D	Pass
TC07	69	Upper boundary of D	Grade D	Pass
TC08	70	Lower boundary of C	Grade C	Pass
TC09	79	Upper boundary of C	Grade C	Pass
TC10	80	Lower boundary of B	Grade B	Pass
TC11	89	Upper boundary of B	Grade B	Pass
TC12	90	Lower boundary of A	Grade A	Pass
TC13	100	Maximum	Grade A	Pass
TC14	101	Above maximum	Invalid marks message	Pass
TC15	abc	Non-numeric value	Invalid marks message	Pass

OUTPUT
Test Execution Summary
Total Designed	Executed	Passed	Failed	Blocked	Pass %
15	15	15	0	0	100%

RESULT
Thus, the test cases of the student grade evaluation system were created using Boundary Value Analysis and the output was verified. Values on and around every boundary were tested.
